.TH SDE-VIEW 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-view \- Photo, the SDE photo viewer and editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-view
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIURI\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Photo shows pictures and edits them. It opens quickly: the preview
embedded in a camera photo (or its cached thumbnail) is shown at once,
then a screen-sized image, then the full image. Photos are shown upright
following their EXIF orientation. Animated GIFs play.
.PP
Photo steps through the other pictures of the folder (in name order), or
through a Gallery album (see
.BR \-\-album ).
A filmstrip shows them below the photo.
.SS Viewing
The mouse wheel (or Ctrl+wheel for finer steps) zooms around the pointer;
drag to move a zoomed photo; double-click switches between best fit and a
closer look. Best Fit, Actual Size (1:1) and Fill Window are in the View
menu. Full screen (F11) and a slideshow (F5) are available.
.SS Information
The information panel (I) shows the file name, folder, size, type,
dimensions and colour profile, and the camera details from EXIF: date
taken, camera, lens, exposure time, aperture, ISO, focal length, flash and
exposure bias. Photos with a GPS position show the coordinates and an
.B Open in Map
link to openstreetmap.org.
.SS Editing
Edits are previewed and kept until saved: rotate (R, Shift+R), flip (H,
V), crop with free or fixed aspect ratios (C), resize, the adjustments
exposure, brightness, contrast, saturation, warmth, fade and vignette, and
the filters Vivid, Warm, Cool, B&W, Noir, Sepia, Vintage, Matte and Invert
with a strength. Every step can be undone and redone.
.PP
Save replaces the file after asking; Save As writes a copy (JPEG, PNG,
WebP or TIFF). A JPEG that was only rotated or flipped is saved without
loss of quality by updating its EXIF orientation. Other edits are encoded
again with the chosen quality; JPEG files keep their camera details.
GIF and SVG pictures are saved as PNG.
.SS Other actions
Copy Image (the clipboard offers PNG data, the file and its path), Set as
Wallpaper, Print (through CUPS
.BR lp ),
Open With another application, Show in Files
.RB ( liria ),
Show in Gallery
.RB ( sde-gallery ),
Add to Favorites (shared with Gallery) and Move to Trash (freedesktop.org
Trash). Changes are announced to a running Gallery, which updates at once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-album= ID
Step through a Gallery album, in Gallery's sort order:
.BR all ,
.BR favorites ,
.BR recent ,
.BR screenshots ,
.BI folder: PATH
(a library folder and its subfolders; a bare absolute path means the
same),
.BI device: PATH
(removable media),
.BI dir: PATH
(one folder) or
.BI list: FILE
(one path per line).
.TP
.BI \-\-sort= ORDER
.BR newest ,
.B oldest
or
.BR name .
.TP
.B \-\-slideshow
Start a slideshow.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start in full screen.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary.
.PP
With several files, Photo steps through exactly those files.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Left, Right, Home, End, Space, Backspace
Previous, next, first, last photo.
.TP
.B + \- 0 1 F
Zoom in, zoom out, best fit, actual size, fill.
.TP
.B R, Shift+R, H, V, C, E
Rotate right or left, flip, crop, edit panel.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Shift+S
Undo, redo, save, save as.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C, Ctrl+D, Ctrl+G, Ctrl+P, Delete
Copy image, favorite, show in Gallery, print, move to the Trash.
.TP
.B I, B, F1, F5, F11, Esc, Ctrl+W
Information, filmstrip, shortcuts, slideshow, full screen, leave, close.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/sde.conf
Section
.B [photo]
keeps
.B jpeg_quality=
(default 92),
.B slideshow_interval=
(seconds),
.B info=
and
.BR filmstrip= .
Favorites are the
.B favorites=
list of
.BR [gallery] ;
Set as Wallpaper writes
.B wallpaper=
in
.BR [appearance] .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-gallery (1),
.BR liria (1),
.BR sde-settings (1)
